\name{FreezeSlicerOrder}
\alias{FreezeSlicerOrder}
\title{An order above the exchange's freeze quantity, split into even orders that each fit}
\description{
An exchange refuses any single futures or options order above its freeze quantity. UBI reads the limit that the broker it is sending to publishes, in that broker's own units, and splits the order into as few orders as fit below it, cut in whole lots as evenly as whole lots allow, so 55 NIFTY lots of 65 under a limit of 3,511 go as 28 and 27 lots. When the broker publishes no limit, the order goes whole, and an order whose single lot is already above the limit is refused with HTTP 400. By default UBI holds the whole order until the other side of the book reaches its price and then sends every slice together, answering HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}; with \code{hold_limits} \code{FALSE} it is sent at once, and the answer carries a \code{legs} list with one entry per slice.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}, and this type adds none of its own.
}
